\# GCE UI Rules

\#\# Purpose

This rule governs every frontend implementation across the GCE platform.

Whenever creating or modifying:

\- Pages  
\- Components  
\- Dashboards  
\- Forms  
\- Layouts  
\- Navigation  
\- Cards  
\- Modals  
\- Tables  
\- Lists

always follow the official UI documentation before writing code.

\---

\# Documentation Priority

Read the following documentation before implementing frontend features.

\#\# Primary UI Documentation

\`\`\`  
13\_UI\_Guidelines.md  
\`\`\`

This document defines the official GCE Design System.

\---

\#\# Component Library

\`\`\`  
34\_Component\_Library.md  
\`\`\`

Always search for an existing reusable component before creating a new one.

Never duplicate UI components.

\---

\#\# UI UX Pro Max

\`\`\`  
28\_UI\_UX\_Pro\_Max\_Expert.md  
\`\`\`

Whenever building or modifying UI, automatically use the UI UX Pro Max AI Skill.

The UI UX Pro Max skill is the primary UX-architecture skill for the GCE platform. It is not the sole design engine. Visual identity remains \`design-system/MASTER.md\`. Taste, Impeccable, and Emil Kowalski skills are advisory craft tools and do not supersede MASTER.

Always generate professional, modern, responsive interfaces that follow the documented GCE Design System.

\---

\#\# Approved Design Tooling

Canonical visual authority is MASTER plus \`lib/frontend/design-language.ts\` and \`lib/frontend/motion.ts\`.

Approved frontend design tooling:

\- MASTER / design-language (visual identity)  
\- ui-ux-pro-max (UX architecture, usability, responsive, accessibility)  
\- ui-styling (Tailwind/CSS implementation)  
\- Taste Skill (anti-slop composition and page hierarchy)  
\- Impeccable (critique, audit, polish)  
\- Emil Kowalski skills (motion and micro-interaction craft)  
\- 21st.dev search-only (structural inspiration)  
\- shadcn primitives (accessibility foundation)

Taste, Impeccable, and Emil augment design judgment. They do not supersede MASTER.

See \`.cursor/rules/09_Design_Tooling_Governance.mdc\`.

\---

