\---

\# UI Philosophy

Every interface should be:

\- Modern  
\- Premium  
\- Clean  
\- Consistent  
\- Mobile First  
\- Responsive  
\- Accessible  
\- Fast

Never create inconsistent UI.

\---

\# Existing Components First

Before creating any component:

Search the project.

If an existing component exists:

Reuse it.

If it is similar:

Extend it.

Never duplicate UI.

\---

\# Component Rules

All components should be:

\- Reusable  
\- Modular  
\- Typed  
\- Configurable  
\- Responsive

Avoid hardcoded values.

Use props.

\---

\# UI UX Pro Max Usage

Whenever generating UI:

Automatically use the UI UX Pro Max AI Skill.

The skill should guide:

\- Layout  
\- Typography  
\- Spacing  
\- Color  
\- Visual Hierarchy  
\- User Experience  
\- Interaction Design

Do not create custom styling that conflicts with the project design system.

\---

\# Motion Usage

Whenever appropriate:

Use Motion for:

\- Hover  
\- Tap  
\- Page Transition  
\- Modal Animation  
\- Card Animation  
\- List Animation  
\- Loading State

Do not overuse animations.

Animations should enhance usability.

\---

\# Responsive Design

Always design for:

1\. Mobile  
2\. Tablet  
3\. Desktop

Never create desktop-only layouts.

\---

\# Design Consistency

Maintain consistency across:

\- Buttons  
\- Cards  
\- Forms  
\- Tables  
\- Navigation  
\- Typography  
\- Colors  
\- Icons  
\- Spacing

The application should feel like one unified product.

\---

\# Forms

Forms should always include:

\- Validation  
\- Error States  
\- Loading State  
\- Success Feedback  
\- Accessible Labels

Never create incomplete forms.

\---

\# Dashboards

Whenever creating dashboards:

Read:

\`\`\`  
12\_Dashboards.md  
\`\`\`

Use:

\- Bento Grid Layout  
\- KPI Cards  
\- Statistics  
\- Charts  
\- Quick Actions

Dashboards should be clean and information-rich.

\---

\# Navigation

Navigation should be:

\- Simple  
\- Predictable  
\- Mobile Friendly

Support:

\- Sidebar  
\- Navbar  
\- Bottom Navigation  
\- Breadcrumbs

\---

\# Accessibility

Every UI should support:

\- Keyboard Navigation  
\- Screen Readers  
\- Focus States  
\- ARIA Labels  
\- Sufficient Contrast

Accessibility is mandatory.

\---

\# Performance

Do not create heavy UI.

Prefer:

\- Lazy Loading  
\- Optimized Images  
\- Efficient Rendering  
\- Small Components

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

\---

\# Tailwind Standards

Use Tailwind CSS consistently.

Avoid inline styles unless absolutely necessary.

Use reusable utility patterns.

\---

\# Icons

Maintain a consistent icon library throughout the project.

Do not mix multiple icon styles.

\---

\# Colors

Always follow the official GCE Design System.

Never introduce random colors.

Use semantic colors for:

\- Success  
\- Warning  
\- Error  
\- Information

\---

\# Typography

Maintain a consistent typography hierarchy.

Do not randomly change:

\- Font Sizes  
\- Font Weights  
\- Line Heights  
\- Letter Spacing

\---

\# Spacing

Maintain a consistent spacing system.

Avoid arbitrary margins and paddings.

\---

\# Empty States

Every empty page should include:

\- Illustration (optional)  
\- Helpful Message  
\- Primary Action

Never leave blank screens.

\---

\# Loading States

Always provide:

\- Skeleton Loaders  
\- Spinners  
\- Progress Indicators

Never leave users waiting without feedback.

\---

\# Error States

Every error should:

\- Explain the problem  
\- Suggest the next step  
\- Match the GCE UI style

\---

\# Before Writing UI

Always verify:

✓ Existing component searched

✓ Component can be reused

✓ UI UX Pro Max applied

✓ Motion considered

✓ Mobile responsive

✓ Accessible

✓ Consistent with Design System

✓ Matches Component Library

\---

\# Forbidden Practices

Never:

\- Duplicate Components  
\- Ignore UI Guidelines  
\- Ignore Component Library  
\- Ignore Motion Standards  
\- Ignore UI UX Pro Max  
\- Hardcode Colors  
\- Hardcode Spacing  
\- Create Inconsistent UI  
\- Build Desktop-Only Interfaces  
\- Use Excessive Animations

\---

\# Final Rule

Every frontend feature should look and behave as if it was designed by the same product design team.

Before generating any frontend code:

1\. Read the relevant UI documentation.  
2\. Search for existing reusable components.  
3\. Apply the UI UX Pro Max AI Skill.  
4\. Follow the Component Library.  
5\. Use Motion where appropriate.  
6\. Produce production-ready, responsive, reusable, and accessible UI.  
